{"task": "WH_8293", "job": "WH_8293|H_c|0", "arm": "H_c", "attempt": 1, "role": "основной", "outcome": "годный", "reason": "годный", "final": "годный", "waits": 0, "retries": 0, "streak": 0, "flags": {"api_retry_до_начала": 0, "api_retry_после_начала": 0, "оборванный_ход": false, "message_start": 1}, "started": "2026-10-26T09:15:36+00:00", "finished": "2026-10-26T09:17:08+00:00", "config_sha256": "4852eb051287b737e790bccbd76bdf753a8dfb80399f9bdbf57966609690d086", "binary_sha256": "27122ca7b624f537546fbef35b80c66370d974ff258f3d9b10ac50bb8771f262", "cli_init_version": "2.1.294", "cli_pinned_version": "2.1.294", "model_target": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_usage_keys": ["claude-opus-5-5"], "model_usage_out": {"claude-opus-5-5": 8550}, "init_sha256": "19a6ffcf0781096cd8fadcc901d1f698c81748761870f4f438dc6f07a56b3d9a", "session_id": "b653d5d5-4bfd-4dcd-b3e4-c09bd32ee93d", "effort": "high", "thinking_budget": "31999", "thinking_tokens": 7375, "env_config": {"API_TIMEOUT_MS": "1200000", "CLAUDE_BYTE_STREAM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS": "180000", "CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC": "1", "CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_RETRIES": "0", "CLAUDE_ENABLE_BYTE_WATCHDOG": "1", "CLAUDE_ENABLE_STREAM_WATCHDOG": "1", "CLAUDE_STREAM_FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT_MS": "180000", "CLAUDE_STREAM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS": "180000", "DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER": "1", "DISABLE_GROWTHBOOK": "1", "MAX_THINKING_TOKENS": "31999"}, "env_access_names": ["ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL", "CLAUDE_CODE_PROXY_RESOLVES_HOSTS", "CLAUDE_SESSION_INGRESS_TOKEN_FILE", "CURL_CA_BUNDLE", "HTTPS_PROXY", "NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS", "NO_PROXY", "PATH", "REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE", "SSL_CERT_FILE", "https_proxy", "no_proxy"], "usage": {"inp": 6174, "out": 8550, "cost_usd": 0.20241280000000003}, "answer": {"choice": 1, "p_best": 0.45}, "exit": {"returncode": 0, "timed_out": false, "stderr_bytes": 0, "stderr_sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855", "spawn_error": null}, "stream": {"file": "WH_8293_H_c_0-0886a93d.a001.osn.jsonl.gz", "sha256": "96bf1c5147693e9de24060c0d137b2d38746a9c8c53c345241a7d1f1ec563501", "bytes": 144516, "lines": 369, "events_no_deltas": [{"type": "system", "subtype": "init", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "tools": ["StructuredOutput"], "mcp_servers": [], "permissionMode": "auto", "claude_code_version": "2.1.294", "output_style": "default", "init_sha256": "19a6ffcf0781096cd8fadcc901d1f698c81748761870f4f438dc6f07a56b3d9a"}, {"type": "system", "subtype": "status", "status": "requesting"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "message_start", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQbUTpwJRzZ87pomQTKP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3868, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3868}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "ttft_ms": 2323, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 0, "content_block": {"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQbUTpwJRzZ87pomQTKP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": {"длина": 21632, "sha256": "23e628e366f2a093d37872c35523089e388a27104b46d9b9442fb47aaed85fa9"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3868, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3868}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T09:16:56.820Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQbUTZp9ArG6fa7UzdtW", "thinking_duration_ms": 77183}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 1, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQbUTpwJRzZ87pomQTKP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I pick **candidate 1**, with p_best = 0.45. This comes from rough mental estimates, not a simulation.\n\n**What all plans share.** The starting stock of good 0 (58 units) runs out by day 1, and nothing new arrives before day 5. Good 1's 27 units also run out on day 1, and its first deliveries come on day 3. So every candidate has roughly the same shortages at the start. The plans differ in how much they order compared with the mean demand. The mean demand is 1.046 × forecast, because the average multiplier is 1.046.\n\n**The key effect is carry-over.** Good 0 keeps for 8 days and good 1 for 4 days, and the oldest stock sells first. So any extra stock rolls into the next days instead of being written off.\n- If a plan orders more than mean demand, stock keeps building. It pays holding every day, and whatever is left on day 29 is wasted purchase money.\n- If a plan orders exactly mean demand, it still runs short sometimes because demand bounces around. But the shortfall only grows with the square root of the number of days: about 50 units of good 0 and about 30 units of good 1 over the whole period.\n\n**Daily plans (candidates 1–5).** They differ mainly in their multiplier on the forecast:\n- Candidate 1 is about 1.05×, almost exactly mean demand.\n- Candidate 3 is about 1.1× for good 0 and about 1.12× for good 1.\n- Candidate 4 is about 1.15–1.2×.\n- Candidate 5 is like candidate 3 for good 0, but about 1.25–1.3× for good 1.\n- Candidate 2 is about 1.25×.\n\nGoing from 1.05× to 1.1× on good 0 adds about 55 units bought. Only about 17 of those turn into extra sales, worth about +340 (selling price plus the avoided penalty). Against that, the extra purchases cost about 330 and the extra holding about 365. That nets out at roughly −350. For good 1, going from 1.05× to 1.12× costs about 470 in extra purchases and recovers only about 220 in sales. So the higher multipliers lose money step by step, and candidate 1 comes out ahead of 3, then 4, then 5 and 2.\n\n**Batch plans:**\n- **Candidate 0** orders every 2 days on 16 days instead of 27. That saves about 363 in order fees. But its order sizes are high (about 1.1× for good 0 and about 1.16× for good 1), which loses about 750 as above. Holding each half-batch an extra day adds about 420 more.\n- **Candidate 7** has the same rhythm as candidate 0 but orders more (about 1.2–1.25×), so it does worse.\n- **Candidate 6** orders every 3 days at about 1.1–1.15×. It saves about 594 in fees, but holding the batches costs roughly 840 extra for good 0 alone.\n\n**Robustness.** Cash and the 228-unit capacity didn't look like binding limits for any plan, as far as I checked. If demand comes in lower than forecast, the plans with bigger safety margins lose even more. If demand comes in higher, they gain a little, but not enough to beat candidate 1 on average. My confidence is moderate because the shortfall figures are rough and candidates 3 and 0 are not far behind."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3868, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3868}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "i